<page type="text">
  <layout>Two columns: a narrow column of marginal notes on the left, and one main text column on the right. The top line is Arabic, followed by the hyphenated word "Praef-" that continues in the next line. Below the text, nothing is printed.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true"><illegible, ~30 letters> Praef-<note side="left">* Propriè trun-cum vel caudi-cem palmæ de-notat.</note><note side="left">v. Alkodai.</note>fectu ingemuit {*}trabs [seu columna lignea] juxta quam priùs orationes habere solitus est, cùm sibi suggestum struxisset; adeò ut omnes socii ipsius vocem, veluti cameli audirent; cùm autem eam ad se recepisset quievit.</p>
    <p><note side="left">l.11.</note>Quòd apud eum quereretur Camelus ] [scil. de durâ, quam serviret, servitute. من كثرة العمل و قلة العلف de laboris copiâ &amp; pabuli inopiâ, quam apud Dominum suum inveniret, ut loquitur <i>Aspahani</i>.</p>
    <p><note side="left">ibid.</note>Quòd ei testimonium perhibuerit ovis assa, cujus armus ipsi dixerit, <i>Cave me comedas, &amp;c.</i> ] At quàm iniquè cum Propheta egit, quòd non priùs ipsi illud dixerit</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The Arabic on the first line is too faint to read letter by letter and is marked illegible. The inline Arabic in the second paragraph is copied as far as it can be read. The asterisk in the text ("*trabs") is the mark for the first left-hand note.</notes>
</page>